{
	title: 'Support both Node and Bun runtimes',
	description: 'Keep ./run as the only launcher for the checkout and installed tsk. Prefer Bun when both runtimes are available. Both npm install -g @anttikissa/tsk on a Node-only system and bun install -g @anttikissa/tsk on a Bun-only system must run tsk. Support Node.js new enough to run .ts files from the checkout; compile JavaScript before packing so installed Node packages work from node_modules without Bun, and exclude stale build output from previous builds.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Node strips types from .ts files in the checkout (Node >= 22.18) but refuses to under node_modules, so the installed package must ship compiled JavaScript (for example tsc to dist/ at prepack) and ./run must choose it when src/ is absent.',
		'A machine with both runtimes hides this; test installed runs with only Node on PATH (see node-only.reference.test.ts).'
	],
	needs: ['tc']
}
